-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online
-- (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every `-- src:` line copies a line of that file.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the
-- Act does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ea3)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- Not encoded as rules: ss 138, 139(1), 139(2)(a) to (g), 139(2)(ga), 139(2B), 139(3), 140 are powers of the Minister
-- to make regulations or orders (machinery; NOTES.md, Coverage).  What those regulations prescribe is an
-- input wherever an earlier provision says "prescribed".

§ `Part 16 -- Procedure and regulations`

§§ `s 127 to s 136`

-- src:5233 | 127. For the purposes of this Act and of the Penal Code 1871, the
-- src:5234 | Commissioner, every other officer appointed or acting under this Act,
-- src:5235 | and every authorised person (when carrying out any function or duty
-- src:5236 | of the Commissioner) are deemed to be public servants within the
-- src:5237 | meaning of the Penal Code 1871.
@ref s 127 (src:5233-5237)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner or another officer appointed or acting under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127 the person is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the Commissioner or another officer appointed or acting under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an authorised person` AND `the person is carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every authorised person (when carrying out any function or duty of the Commissioner)" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"): an authorised person who is not carrying out one is outside the deeming
        IF `the person is an authorised person` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of the Commissioner, every other officer appointed or acting under the Act, and every authorised person carrying out the Commissioner's function; the Act does not say another person is not deemed a public servant (ruling (c), 2026-11-05)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5246 | 127A. No liability shall lie against any person appointed under
-- src:5247 | section 3 or any other person acting under the direction of the
-- src:5248 | Commissioner for anything which is done with reasonable care and in
-- src:5249 | good faith in the execution or purported execution of this Act.
@ref s 127A (src:5246-5249)
GIVEN `the person was appointed under section 3 or is acting under the direction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done with reasonable care and in good faith in the execution or purported execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127A liability lies against the person` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed under section 3 or is acting under the direction of the Commissioner` AND `the thing was done with reasonable care and in good faith in the execution or purported execution of this Act`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No liability shall lie against any person appointed under section 3 or any other person acting under the direction of the Commissioner for anything which is done with reasonable care and in good faith"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for what is done with reasonable care and in good faith; the Act does not say whether liability lies for anything else
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5255 | 128. For the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control
-- src:5256 | (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015, every place of employment is
-- src:5257 | deemed to be a public place.
@ref s 128 (src:5255-5257)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "place of employment"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 2(1) "place of employment"` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of "every place of employment"; the Act does not say a place that is not one is not a public place
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same deeming with its purpose asked: "For the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015"
-- is a scope limit with no "only" (ruling (c), 2026-11-05), so for any other purpose the Act is silent.
-- src:5255 | 128. For the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control
-- src:5256 | (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015, every place of employment is
-- src:5257 | deemed to be a public place.
@ref s 128 (src:5255-5257)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "place of employment"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purpose` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 2(1) "place of employment"` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the purpose is section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015, every place of employment is deemed to be a public place"; for any other purpose the Act does not deem it one and does not say it is not (ruling (c), 2026-11-05)
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 129(1) Complainant` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(1) a person aggrieved`
    `s 129(1) the Commissioner`
    `s 129(1) a person authorised by the Commissioner in that behalf`
    `s 129(1) some other person`

-- src:5263 | 129.—(1) Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this
-- src:5264 | Act, all convictions and penalties for offences under this Act may be
-- src:5265 | had and recovered before a Magistrate’s Court or a District Court on
-- src:5266 | complaint by any person aggrieved or by the Commissioner or any
-- src:5267 | person authorised by the Commissioner in that behalf.
@ref s 129(1) (src:5263-5267)
GIVEN court IS A `Official or body the Act names`
      complainant IS A `s 129(1) Complainant`
      `a special provision to the contrary in this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this Act" leaves the answer to that other provision
        IF `a special provision to the contrary in this Act applies` THEN NOTHING
        IF (court EQUALS `Body: a Magistrate's Court` OR court EQUALS `Body: a District Court`) AND complainant EQUALS `s 129(1) a person aggrieved` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (court EQUALS `Body: a Magistrate's Court` OR court EQUALS `Body: a District Court`) AND complainant EQUALS `s 129(1) the Commissioner` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (court EQUALS `Body: a Magistrate's Court` OR court EQUALS `Body: a District Court`) AND complainant EQUALS `s 129(1) a person authorised by the Commissioner in that behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 129(1) names the two courts and the three complainants; it does not say that no other court or complainant will do
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5269 | (2) A Magistrate’s Court or a District Court may, despite anything
-- src:5270 | in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, impose the full punishment
-- src:5271 | prescribed by this Act, except that a Magistrate’s Court is not to
-- src:5272 | impose a sentence of imprisonment exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 129(2) (src:5269-5272)
GIVEN court IS A `Official or body the Act names`
      `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(2) the court may impose the term of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Body: a Magistrate's Court` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment in months` GREATER THAN 12
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a Magistrate's Court is not to impose a sentence of imprisonment exceeding 12 months"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Body: a District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 129(2) is about a Magistrate's Court and a District Court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5269 | (2) A Magistrate’s Court or a District Court may, despite anything
-- src:5270 | in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, impose the full punishment
-- src:5271 | prescribed by this Act, except that a Magistrate’s Court is not to
-- src:5272 | impose a sentence of imprisonment exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 129(2) (src:5269-5272)
GIVEN court IS A `Official or body the Act names`
      `the longest term of imprisonment the Act prescribes for the offence, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Body: a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (min `the longest term of imprisonment the Act prescribes for the offence, in months` 12)
    WHEN `Body: a District Court` THEN JUST `the longest term of imprisonment the Act prescribes for the offence, in months`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 129(2) is about a Magistrate's Court and a District Court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5276 | 130. The Commissioner and any officer authorised by the
-- src:5277 | Commissioner in writing have the right to appear and be heard
-- src:5278 | before a Magistrate’s Court or a District Court in any proceedings
-- src:5279 | under this Act and also have the right to be heard before those Courts
-- src:5280 | in any prosecution under Chapter 16 of the Penal Code 1871
-- src:5281 | instituted by him or her in accordance with section 125.
@ref s 130 (src:5276-5281)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner or an officer authorised by the Commissioner in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A `Official or body the Act names`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130 the person has the right to appear and be heard` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Commissioner or an officer authorised by the Commissioner in writing` AND (court EQUALS `Body: a Magistrate's Court` OR court EQUALS `Body: a District Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is of the Commissioner and an officer authorised in writing, before a Magistrate's Court or a District Court
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5285 | 131. In all proceedings under Part 15, the onus of proving that a
-- src:5286 | person is not the employer or the person whose duty it is under this
-- src:5287 | Act to do or abstain from doing anything is on the person who alleges
-- src:5292 | that the person is not the employer or other person, as the case may
-- src:5293 | be.
@ref s 131 (src:5285-5293)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person alleges that the person is not the employer or the person whose duty it is under this Act to do or abstain from doing anything` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131 the onus of proving that the person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under Part 15` AND `the person alleges that the person is not the employer or the person whose duty it is under this Act to do or abstain from doing anything`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the onus is placed in "all proceedings under Part 15" on the person who makes that allegation; the Act places no other onus here
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Fork F23: "in any case in which proceedings are not instituted, or, if instituted, are not proceeded with to judgment
-- under this Act" is read as the condition under which the preservation applies.
-- src:5297 | 132. Nothing in this Act operates to prevent any employer or
-- src:5298 | employee from enforcing the employer’s or employee’s respective
-- src:5299 | civil rights and remedies for any breach or non‑performance of a
-- src:5300 | contract of service by any suit in court in any case in which
-- src:5301 | proceedings are not instituted, or, if instituted, are not proceeded with
-- src:5302 | to judgment under this Act.
@ref s 132 (src:5297-5302)
GIVEN `proceedings under this Act are not instituted or, if instituted, are not proceeded with to judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132 this Act prevents the employer or employee from enforcing civil rights and remedies by suit in court` MEANS
    IF `proceedings under this Act are not instituted or, if instituted, are not proceeded with to judgment`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act operates to prevent any employer or employee from enforcing the employer's or employee's respective civil rights and remedies"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): where proceedings under this Act were proceeded with to judgment, section 132 does not say whether a suit is open
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5306 | 133. Where the Commissioner or any officer performing the duties
-- src:5307 | or exercising the powers conferred on the Commissioner has, for the
-- src:5308 | purpose of inquiring into any matter under this Act, taken down any
-- src:5309 | evidence or made any memorandum and is prevented by death,
-- src:5310 | transfer or other cause from concluding the inquiry, any successor to
-- src:5311 | the Commissioner or other officer may deal with the evidence or
-- src:5312 | memorandum as if the successor had taken it down or made it and
-- src:5313 | proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which his or her
-- src:5314 | predecessor left it.
@ref s 133 (src:5306-5314)
GIVEN `the predecessor has taken down evidence or made a memorandum for the purpose of inquiring into a matter under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the predecessor is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from concluding the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133 the successor may proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which the predecessor left it` MEANS
    IF `the predecessor has taken down evidence or made a memorandum for the purpose of inquiring into a matter under this Act` AND `the predecessor is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from concluding the inquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioner or any officer ... has, for the purpose of inquiring into any matter under this Act, taken down any evidence or made any memorandum and is prevented by death, transfer or other cause from concluding the inquiry" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): with either not so the power is not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `s 134 Recipient of the fine` IS ONE OF
    `s 134 the party complaining`
    `s 134 the employee, where the offence was committed by an employer in respect of a liability to pay money to that employee`
    `s 134 some other person`

-- src:5318 | 134. When under this Act any court imposes a fine or enforces the
-- src:5319 | payment of any sum secured by a recognizance or bond, the court
-- src:5320 | may direct that the whole or any part of the fine or sum when
-- src:5321 | recovered be paid to the party complaining, or where the offence was
-- src:5322 | committed by an employer in respect of a liability to pay money to an
-- src:5323 | employee, that employee.
@ref s 134 (src:5318-5323)
GIVEN `the court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of a sum secured by a recognizance or bond under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `s 134 Recipient of the fine`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When under this Act any court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of any sum secured by a recognizance or bond, the court may direct" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"): without a fine or a sum so enforced the court has no such power
        IF NOT `the court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of a sum secured by a recognizance or bond under this Act` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 134 the party complaining` OR recipient EQUALS `s 134 the employee, where the offence was committed by an employer in respect of a liability to pay money to that employee` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the direction is to the party complaining, or to the employee where the offence was an employer's failure to pay money to that employee; the Act does not say the court may not direct it elsewhere
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5327 | 135. Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this Act,
