      `a special provision to the contrary in this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135 the amount ordered is deemed to be liquidated and discharged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this Act" leaves the answer to that other provision
        IF `a special provision to the contrary in this Act applies` THEN NOTHING
        IF `imprisonment has been suffered under this Act for non-payment of the amount of a fine, compensation or damages, with the costs assessed and directed to be paid by an order of court, and has been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming follows the determination of imprisonment suffered for non-payment
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5327 | 135. Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this Act,
