        IF `a special provision to the contrary in this Act applies` THEN NOTHING
        IF `imprisonment has been suffered under this Act for non-payment of the amount of a fine, compensation or damages, with the costs assessed and directed to be paid by an order of court, and has been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5339 | 136. In the event of any employer being subjected to any fine or
-- src:5340 | penalty (but not an administrative penalty under Part 15A) under the
-- src:5341 | provisions of this Act, the fine or penalty may, in addition to any other
-- src:5342 | means of recovery, be recovered by distress and sale of the place of
-- src:5343 | employment, or of any property belonging to the employer and in the
-- src:5344 | place of employment.
@ref s 136 (src:5339-5344)
GIVEN `the employer has been subjected to a fine or penalty under the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is an administrative penalty under Part 15A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136 the fine or penalty may be recovered by distress and sale of the place of employment or property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the penalty is an administrative penalty under Part 15A` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any fine or penalty (but not an administrative penalty under Part 15A)"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the employer has been subjected to a fine or penalty under the provisions of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of any employer being subjected to any fine or penalty (but not an administrative penalty under Part 15A) under the provisions of this Act, the fine or penalty may ... be recovered by distress and sale" ("in the event of" read as "where", assumed not ruled, fork F28)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 137 Service of requisitions and summons`

DECLARE `s 137(1) Way of serving` IS ONE OF
    `s 137(1)(a) delivering it to the person or to some adult member of the person's family at the person's last known place of residence`
    `s 137(1)(b) leaving it at, or sending it by registered post to, the person's usual or last known place of residence or business in an envelope addressed to the person`
    `s 137(1)(c)(i) delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body at its registered office or principal place of business`
    `s 137(1)(c)(ii) sending it by registered post addressed to the body at its registered office or principal place of business`
    `s 137(1) some other way`

-- src:5350 | 137.—(1) Any requisition issued under section 98 or 99 or any
-- src:5351 | summons issued under section 116, 119 or 124 may be served on any
-- src:5352 | person —
-- src:5354 | (a) by delivering it to the person or to some adult member of
-- src:5355 | his or her family at his or her last known place of residence;
-- src:5357 | (b) by leaving it at or sending it by registered post to the
-- src:5358 | person’s usual or last known place of residence or business
-- src:5359 | in an envelope addressed to the person; or
-- src:5361 | (c) where the person is a body of persons or a body
-- src:5362 | corporate —
-- src:5364 | (i) by delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or
-- src:5365 | other similar officer of the body of persons or body
-- src:5366 | corporate at its registered office or principal place of
-- src:5367 | business; or
-- src:5369 | (ii) by sending it by registered post addressed to the body
-- src:5370 | of persons or body corporate at its registered office or
-- src:5371 | principal place of business.
@ref s 137(1) (src:5350-5371)
GIVEN way IS A `s 137(1) Way of serving`
      `the person is a body of persons or a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 137(1)(a) delivering it to the person or to some adult member of the person's family at the person's last known place of residence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 137(1)(b) leaving it at, or sending it by registered post to, the person's usual or last known place of residence or business in an envelope addressed to the person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 137(1)(c)(i) delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body at its registered office or principal place of business` THEN
        IF `the person is a body of persons or a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) where the person is a body of persons or a body corporate" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `s 137(1)(c)(ii) sending it by registered post addressed to the body at its registered office or principal place of business` THEN
        IF `the person is a body of persons or a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 137(1) says a requisition or summons "may be served" in three ways and does not say it may be served in no other
    WHEN `s 137(1) some other way` THEN NOTHING

-- src:5373 | (2) Any requisition or summons sent by registered post to any
-- src:5374 | person in accordance with subsection (1) is deemed to be duly served
-- src:5375 | on the person at the time when the requisition or summons (as the
-- src:5376 | case may be) would in the ordinary course of post be delivered and, in
-- src:5377 | proving service of the requisition or summons, it is sufficient to prove
-- src:5378 | that the envelope containing the requisition or summons (as the case
-- src:5379 | may be) was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered
-- src:5380 | post.
@ref s 137(2) (src:5373-5380)
GIVEN `it was sent by registered post to the person in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 137(2) the requisition or summons sent by registered post is deemed to be duly served at the time` MEANS
    IF `it was sent by registered post to the person in accordance with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST `the day on which it would in the ordinary course of post be delivered`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of a requisition or summons "sent by registered post to any person in accordance with subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5377 | proving service of the requisition or summons, it is sufficient to prove
-- src:5378 | that the envelope containing the requisition or summons (as the case
-- src:5379 | may be) was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered
-- src:5380 | post.
@ref s 137(2) (src:5377-5380)
GIVEN `the envelope was properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the envelope was properly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the envelope was posted by registered post` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(2) it is sufficient to prove that the envelope was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered post` MEANS
    IF `the envelope was properly addressed` AND `the envelope was properly stamped` AND `the envelope was posted by registered post`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): it is "sufficient" to prove those three things; the Act does not say that proof of anything less fails
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 139 Power to make regulations: the ceilings`

-- src:5462 | (h) prescribe the administrative penalties for civil
-- src:5463 | contraventions under Part 15A of an amount not
-- src:5464 | exceeding $1,000 for each occasion of a civil
-- src:5465 | contravention, and $2,000 in the case of a second or
-- src:5466 | subsequent occasion of the civil contravention.
@ref s 139(2)(h) (src:5462-5466)
GIVEN `the occasion is a second or subsequent occasion of the civil contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 139(2)(h) the greatest administrative penalty the regulations may prescribe for the occasion` MEANS
    IF `the occasion is a second or subsequent occasion of the civil contravention`
    THEN 2000
    ELSE 1000

-- Fork F12: a conviction that is neither a first conviction nor a repeat within one year of the preceding one (a second
-- conviction more than a year after the first) is in neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b), so the text gives it no ceiling.
-- src:5470 | (2A) The Minister may, in making any regulations under this Act,
-- src:5471 | provide that any contravention of the provisions of the regulations
-- src:5472 | shall be an offence punishable with a fine not exceeding —
-- src:5474 | (a) $5,000 in the case of a first conviction; and
-- src:5476 | (b) $10,000 in the case of a second or subsequent conviction
-- src:5477 | for contravening or failing to comply with the same
-- src:5482 | provision within one year after the immediately preceding
-- src:5483 | conviction.
@ref s 139(2A) (src:5470-5483)
GIVEN `the day of the immediately preceding conviction for contravening or failing to comply with the same provision, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of the conviction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 139(2A) the greatest fine the regulations may provide for the contravention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day of the immediately preceding conviction for contravening or failing to comply with the same provision, if there was one`
    -- (a): $5,000 "in the case of a first conviction"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 5000
    WHEN JUST preceding THEN
        IF `the day of the conviction` AT MOST (`add years` preceding 1)
        -- (b): $10,000 "in the case of a second or subsequent conviction for contravening or failing to comply with the same provision within one year after the immediately preceding conviction"
        THEN JUST 10000
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a second or subsequent conviction more than one year after the preceding one is in neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b)
        ELSE NOTHING
